{"id":"neet-2025-q046","pn":46,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Structure of Atom","st":"Hydrogen spectrum transitions","q":"The ratio of the wavelengths of the light absorbed by a Hydrogen atom when it undergoes n = 2 → n = 3 and n = 4 → n = 6 transitions, respectively, is","o":["1/36","1/16","1/9","1/4"],"c":3,"s":"ΔE = hc/λ = E_final − E_initial, with E_n = −R_H/n².\nΔE(2→3) = hc/λ(2→3) = E₃ − E₂ = −R_H/3² − (−R_H/2²).\n= R_H(1/4 − 1/9) = R_H × 5/36.\nSo λ(2→3) = hc·36/(R_H·5).\nΔE(4→6) = E₆ − E₄ = −R_H/36 + R_H/16 = R_H × 20/(36 × 16).\nhc/λ(4→6) = R_H × 20/(36 × 16).\nλ(4→6) = hc × 36 × 16/(R_H·20).\nλ(2→3)/λ(4→6) = [hc·36/(R_H·5)] / [hc × 36 × 16/(R_H·20)] = 1/4."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q050","pn":50,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Structure of Atom","st":"Bohr model energy and radius","q":"Energy and radius of first Bohr orbit of He⁺ and Li²⁺ are\n[Given R_H = 2.18 × 10⁻¹⁸ J, a₀ = 52.9 pm]","o":["Eₙ(Li²⁺) = −19.62 × 10⁻¹⁸ J; rₙ(Li²⁺) = 17.6 pm; Eₙ(He⁺) = −8.72 × 10⁻¹⁸ J; rₙ(He⁺) = 26.4 pm","Eₙ(Li²⁺) = −8.72 × 10⁻¹⁸ J; rₙ(Li²⁺) = 26.4 pm; Eₙ(He⁺) = −19.62 × 10⁻¹⁸ J; rₙ(He⁺) = 17.6 pm","Eₙ(Li²⁺) = −19.62 × 10⁻¹⁶ J; rₙ(Li²⁺) = 17.6 pm; Eₙ(He⁺) = −8.72 × 10⁻¹⁶ J; rₙ(He⁺) = 26.4 pm","Eₙ(Li²⁺) = −8.72 × 10⁻¹⁶ J; rₙ(Li²⁺) = 17.6 pm; Eₙ(He⁺) = −19.62 × 10⁻¹⁶ J; rₙ(He⁺) = 17.6 pm"],"c":0,"s":"Eₙ = (−2.18 × 10⁻¹⁸ × z²)/n² J and rₙ = (52.9 × n²)/z pm.\nFor He⁺ (z = 2, n = 1): E = −2.18 × 10⁻¹⁸ × 4 = −8.72 × 10⁻¹⁸ J.\nr(He⁺) = (52.9 × 1)/2 = 26.45 pm.\nFor Li²⁺ (z = 3, n = 1): E = −2.18 × 10⁻¹⁸ × 9 = 19.62 × 10⁻¹⁸ J (sign minus omitted in print).\nr(Li²⁺) = (52.9 × 1)/3 = 17.63 pm.\nNote: Publisher's working writes Li²⁺ energy as 19.62 × 10⁻¹⁸ J without the minus sign; option (1) has the minus sign"}
